OL,3,GNEWSABluetongue restriction zone
OL,4,Aextension a 'positive thing' for
OL,5,Afarmers
OL,6,
OL,7,FRestrictions aimed at controlling
OL,8,Fbluetongue, a virus that affects sheep,
OL,9,Fcattle and other livestock, are now in
OL,10,Fforce across the whole of Scotland.
OL,12,FThe Scottish government said they
OL,13,Fshould be seen as a "positive thing"
OL,14,Fwhich would make it easier for farmers
OL,15,Fto get uninfected animals to market
OL,16,Fwithout requiring an individual
OL,17,Flicence.
OL,19,FThe disease, which can be spread by
OL,20,Finsects such as midges, does not affect
OL,21,Fpeople and poses no risk to food
OL,22,Fsafety.
OL,23,APub: 03-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,430,420,260,160,0,100
